2. DEC — Delphi Encryption Compendium 3.0
================================================================================

Absolute Database's ABSCipher unit is a fork of DEC 3.0 Part I. Three of its
ciphers deviate from the published algorithms, and files written with them
cannot be read by a correct implementation, so rijndael.go, twofish.go,
tdes.go and square.go reproduce DEC's behaviour rather than the specifications.

Those four files are independent Go implementations written from the published
algorithm descriptions (Rijndael/AES, Twofish, DES, and the 1997
Daemen/Knudsen/Rijmen Square cipher). What is owed to DEC is factual rather
than expressive: the knowledge of where DEC deviates, and the self-test vectors
its ciphers carry, which this project's tests use to pin those deviations. DEC
3.0's terms ask only that the copyright be carried, and it is carried here.

